---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { app, studio } from '../../../apps';

const hasha = app('hasha');
// Written from the app as built (Hasha 2.0): no network code, no SDKs, the saved search in UserDefaults,
// and PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy declaring no tracking and no collected data. Update it if any of that changes.
const updated = '28 October 2026';
---
<Base title="Hasha privacy policy" description="Hasha collects no data: no account, no analytics, no tracking and no network access. Everything stays on your device." app={hasha}>
  <section class="container section">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="muted updated">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <div class="card summary">
      <h2>In short</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Hasha collects no data about you.</li>
        <li>It has no account, no ads, no analytics and no tracking.</li>
        <li>It never connects to the internet. Every hash is computed on your device.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What Hasha stores</h2>
      <p>Hasha saves your settings (bit length, CPU or GPU, and seed) and the search in progress, so a search can resume after a pause or relaunch. This is stored only on your device, in the app’s own storage. It may be included in your device backup (iCloud or your computer) under your backup settings. Deleting the app deletes it.</p>

      <h2>What Hasha sends</h2>
      <p>Nothing. The app has no network access, no third-party code and no advertising or analytics tools. Values you copy from the collision screen go only to your clipboard.</p>

      <h2>Information Apple provides</h2>
      <p>If you turned on Share With App Developers in your device’s settings, Apple may share anonymous crash reports and usage statistics with us. Apple collects these, not Hasha, and they don’t identify you. App Store downloads and ratings are handled by Apple under <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple’s privacy policy</a>.</p>

      <h2>Contacting us</h2>
      <p>If you email us, we use your email address and message only to reply. We don’t share them.</p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>Hasha collects no data from anyone, including children.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If this policy changes, we’ll update this page and the date above. If Hasha ever starts collecting data, we’ll say so here before the version that does is released.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>{studio.name}, <a href={`mailto:${studio.email}`}>{studio.email}</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
<style>
  .updated { margin-top: 12px; }
  .summary { margin: 32px 0 8px; max-width: 42em; }
  .summary h2 { font-size: 1.1875rem; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .summary ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.2em; }
  .summary li { margin: 6px 0; }
</style>
